"P2878854754" "Time's Arrow"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Divination 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3077134593" "Divination"
// DetailString :
"P795346087" "As Sister Solaris hovered in the air above you she recited these words...<br><br><color orange><span align=center>Time is not our own... <br>...the arrow flies to the quiver.<br><br>Beasts of metal, flesh and darkness<br>merge to create an army of night<br>spreading its pitch from horizon to horizon.<br><br>Only travelers out of time<br> can hope to die by dawn's first light.</span></color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WhyAmIHere 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4265924718" "Requiem's Journal"
// DetailString :
"P842661295" "After you defeat Requiem, you pull from him a small black journal. Reading through it you find it is entirely in some sort of code that only he can understand. Just as you think you're not going to get anything out of him, Requiem begins to talk...<br><br><color LightSeaGreen><i>I have come across time itself to this land. Our temporal strongholds are growing even now as you stand here gloating. You think you have won, but that is only because you are ignorant to my plans.<br><br> I came here to establish another stronghold in Cimerora. This cradle of power is to be my training ground for recruits. The Cimerorans are the best fighters time has ever seen. They shall be mine.<br><br>Nothing you can do now or later will ever stop me.</i></color><br><br>With those words Requiem teleports away to an unknown location."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1454422779" "Time's Arrow"
// DetailString :
"P34584761" "Imperious once ruled over a land called Cimerora. You traveled through an Ouroboros crystal, hidden within the halls of the Midnighter Club to get to that land and sought out Imperious. He said that a man by the name of Romulus Augustus had deposed him, killing his people and forcing them to the edge of not just his lands, but of survival.<br><br>Your arrival was foretold by the oracle and Romulus commanded you to seek her out at Phoebas Point to divine your next move. However, once you arrived, you found Romulus' men were already there, holding the Sybils captive. At the very top of the mountain, you found Sister Solaris imprisoned by a Minotaur. It wasn't until you had defeated the beast that the sister was able to reach the altar and divine your fate.<br><br><color orange><span align=center>Time is not our own... <br>...the arrow flies to the quiver.<br><br>Beasts of metal, flesh and darkness<br>merge to create an army of night<br>spreading its pitch from horizon to horizon.<br><br>Only travelers out of time<br> can hope to die by dawn's first light.</span></color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1040660970" "Imperious once ruled over a land called Cimerora. You traveled through an Ouroboros crystal, hidden within the halls of the Midnighter Club to get to that land and sought out Imperious. He said that a man by the name of Romulus Augustus had deposed him, killing his people and forcing them to the edge of not just his lands, but of survival.<br><br>Your arrival was foretold by the oracle and Romulus commanded you to seek her out at Phoebas Point to divine your next move. However, once you arrived, you found Romulus' men were already there, holding the Sybils captive. At the very top of the mountain, you found Sister Solaris imprisoned by a Minotaur. It wasn't until you had defeated the beast that the sister was able to reach the altar and divine your fate.<br><br><color orange><span align=center>Time is not our own... <br>...the arrow flies to the quiver.<br><br>Beasts of metal, flesh and darkness<br>merge to create an army of night<br>spreading its pitch from horizon to horizon.<br><br>Only travelers out of time<br> can hope to die by dawn's first light.</span></color><br><br>The appearance of the Nictus at the top of the mountain led you into the caves deep beneath the city. There, these 'dark ones', as Imperious called them, were building their forces. They were being kept alive through multiple shadow cysts hidden within the caves. Destroying these cysts was the key to keeping the Nictus out of this land. However, they were guarded by more Minotaurs as well as giant Cyclops."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P672041443" "Imperious once ruled over a land called Cimerora. You traveled through an Ouroboros crystal, hidden within the halls of the Midnighter Club to get to that land and sought out Imperious. He said that a man by the name of Romulus Augustus had deposed him, killing his people and forcing them to the edge of not just his lands, but of survival.<br><br>Your arrival was foretold by the oracle and Romulus commanded you to seek her out at Phoebas Point to divine your next move. However, once you arrived, you found Romulus' men were already there, holding the Sybils captive. At the very top of the mountain, you found Sister Solaris imprisoned by a Minotaur. It wasn't until you had defeated the beast that the sister was able to reach the altar and divine your fate.<br><br><color orange><span align=center>Time is not our own... <br>...the arrow flies to the quiver.<br><br>Beasts of metal, flesh and darkness<br>merge to create an army of night<br>spreading its pitch from horizon to horizon.<br><br>Only travelers out of time<br> can hope to die by dawn's first light.</span></color><br><br>The appearance of the Nictus atop the mountain, led you into the caves deep beneath the city. There, these 'dark ones', as Imperious called them, were building their forces. They were being kept alive through multiple shadow cysts hidden within the caves. Destroying these cysts was the key to keeping the Nictus out of this land. However, they were guarded by more Minotaurs as well as giant Cyclops.<br><br>With the Nictus taken care of and the morale of Romulus' remaining forces depleted, now was your time to strike directly at the heart Romulus. He had taken over the inner city of Cimerora, Castellum Quarter and was using it as his base of operations. You stormed the gates, but as you got inside, what you found was completely unexpected.<br><br>The 5th Column were here, in ancient Cimerora, commanding Romulus' forces. They were being led by Requiem himself. You overheard talks of invading other times and establishing temporal strongholds. You faced off against Requiem and the entire personal guard of Romulus, only to have the tyrannical emperor come off of his throne to face you. You might not have believed in demi-gods before you fought such a being as Romulus, but you do now. You look back on that battle and wonder how you ever survived."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL9_CP_Imperious_TF 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P2351111959" "You look down at the broken helm of your enemy and are reminded of the events you've come to know as...<br><br><color deepskyblue>Time's Arrow</color><br>Romulus Augustus was once the tyrannical emperor of a land called Cimerora. He took the throne from Imperious, the rightful leader, through the help of the <color red>5th Column</color> and the </color red>Nictus</color>.<br><br>In exchange for their support, Romulus gave his new subjects to the 5th Column and the Nictus to do with what they would. This group’s end goal was to establish temporal strongholds throughout time. Their primary assault was to be on Paragon City and the Rogue Isles. They had built giant colossi that could only be powered by what they called <color orange>Incarnates</color>. The two Incarnates they had in mind were the Honoree and Lord Recluse. If these colossi were brought to life, there would be nothing that would stop them from taking over all of time.<br><br>You arrived to the staging ground just as Romulus Augustus joined with the Nictus. The combined power was more than you had ever faced in a single person. Romulus fought with all the dark forces of the Nictus and, in the end, you wondered what forces must have been coursing through your veins to stop him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RequiemTimeTravelClue06 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1026469962" "Dear {HeroName}..."
// DetailString :
"P263661331" "While time traveling into the past, you visit Cimerora and in a crate you find a hand-written letter addressed to {HeroName}...<br><br>Did you think I wouldn’t find you? You were sly, using an Aspect of the Pillar that wasn’t linked to Ouroboros. Did you ever stop to think where Montague may have acquired that crystal? Or how?<br><br>I apologize. This letter was not meant for harsh words or recriminations. I merely meant to remind you that I can find you...anytime, anyplace, anywhere. That is all.<br><br>Who am I? I know you have been asking yourself that question for a time now. Am I Requiem? Am I Silos? Am I...you, perhaps? You may even be asking yourself which one of those people I am. Have you ever met Praetorian Earth Requiem? He doesn’t go by that name, of course, in case you were wondering. Have you, perchance, met the shadow version of yourself?  What about the version of Mender Silos from Faathim’s reality?<br><br>It is a paradox.<br><br>Try not to think about it.<br><br>But again, my train of thought wanders. I’m writing you to tell you that, as surprising as it might sound, Mender Silos and his time travelling cohorts are actually succeeding in delaying the coming storm. Note, I didn’t say preventing. There is still hope.<br><br>Because of their actions, and likely yours as well, it may be sometime before I can truly extend my hand to you in kinship. There is other work in other places for us to do. As much as I enjoy these letters, I’m sure you will understand that we have more pressing matters to attend. So, for now, I bid you farewell.<br><br>As always, look for me in the crystal."

