// Description :
"P3677235310" "Defeat Romulus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2497419460" "You've defeated Romulus Augustus."
// Script Variable MISSION_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1134671029" "To Romulus!  We must protect him!"
// Script Variable MISSION_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P3636653625" "Rally to him, men!  The travelers will fall!"
// Script Variable MISSION_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1846614885" "Protect Romulus!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P6540317" "You've defeated Romulus Augustus and stopped their attack on Paragon City and the Rogue Isles."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3561075492" "With Romulus defeated and his forces scattered to the winds, it is only a matter of time before Cimerora is once again ours.<br><br>Tell me, who is this 5th Column you discovered in Vespillos Pass? Are they allied with the dark ones? What are they doing here? I fear I have more questions than answers, my friend.<br><br>They must have been the ones supplying Romulus with the weapons and forces he needed to take my empire. There is no way he would have had the power to do it alone.<br><br>Romulus attempted to take over your land and I have heard that they already control many others. Frankly, these actions are beyond his grasp. Romulus never had any grander endeavors beyond what he could hold in his hand. It is obvious that he was merely a pawn in this game, and my land only the board upon which it was played. Be thankful that your own time and place were not subjected to such an atrocity."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3539373940" "Before you arrived, I had hoped that I would be able to retake my own city, but that has not been the case. Since your arrival, you have systematically removed one obstacle after another. Now, only a single block remains before this land is once again returned to its rightful ruler.<br><br>I need your help and you have proven that, above all, you are the ones to help me.<br><br><color orange>Gather your forces; it is time to reclaim the city! The time for subtlety is no more! Now we storm the gates!</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P2318545574" "Retake the city"
// SendOffString :
"P4051099025" "I will be joining you on this assault. It is my home; if anyone should be by your side, it should be me.<br><br>But I have some grave news for you. <color orange>It would appear that somehow Romulus survived your battle at Vespillos Pass.</color> He is guarded by his entire remaining army. The battle will be a fierce one, but I promise you, it will end with Romulus tasting my blade one inch at a time."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P555046986" "Reclaim Cimerora"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1191278823" "Gather your forces and storm the gates of Castellum Quarter! I will meet you on the other side of the wall. We will paint the earth with Romulus' blood!"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3074523284" "<color deepskyblue>Castellum Quarter</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P141128264" "It is only fitting that the final battle against Romulus happens here, at the heart of Cimerora."
// Script Variable DisplayText :
"P2758755854" "traitors to defeat"
// Script Variable DisplayText :
"P847240338" "Defeat Romulus & Minions"
// Script Variable PET_NAME :
"P1039114360" "Imperious"
// Script Variable PET_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2294684788" "<em point>Come!<em>Let us paint the stones red with the blood of our enemies!"
// Script Variable PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P3657495983" "I do not trust these strangers."
// Script Variable PATROLLER2_SEARCHING_DIALOG :
"P1002286221" "With the amount they are paying me, I would trust Hades himself."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2898164479" "General Gabinius"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3123368975" "<shout>Many of you may look at what we have conquered and believe there is nothing left to take.<em>You would be wrong!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1554099138" "General Domitius"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2653596073" "<shout>I have spoken with Romulus and our new allies.  There are many more lands for us to claim."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P4129116194" "General Ursius"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P226866787" "<shout>You may think I am into my cups, the gods know I usually am...<em>...but I am telling you that the gods are on our side."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P623928469" "General Terentius"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2619984080" "<shout>If I hear one more word about our new allies being from beyond the veil, I will rip out the tongue of the who tries!<em>DO YOU HEAR ME!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P4024471798" "General Coruncanius"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P1109217697" "<shout>If any of you have doubts about my ability, please take it up with Romulus.<em>He has an ironic way with traitors."
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2137836638" "General Sergius"

